Hi everyone,

Apologies for the delay on this. I did not want to put dates in writing until
the enviroment position was confirmed, and it was confirmed on Friday evening,
so here we are.

UAT runs Monday 12 October 2026 to Friday 06 November 2026. Sign off is due on
06-Nov. I will chase all of you for it and I am sorry about that in advance.

Scripts. There are 14, UAT-01 to UAT-14. Nine testers between the four teams.
Each script has one named signer, and one person can sign more than one script,
which is why the list below looks lopsided.

  UAT-01 / UAT-02 / UAT-03  D01 Primary Sales Performance     signer: Vikram
  UAT-04 / UAT-05           D03 Distributor Scorecard          signer: Vikram
  UAT-06 / UAT-07 / UAT-08  D07 Revenue Reconciliation         signer: Shalini
  UAT-09 / UAT-10           D09 Product Mix and Contribution   signer: Priya
  UAT-11 to UAT-14          cross checks and the RLS walk       signer: TBC

UAT-11 to UAT-14 are the ones nobody has claimed. Shalini, can I put Meghna's
name against UAT-13 and UAT-14 for the row count checks, or is she already
committed elsewhere that fortnight? Meghna, shout if that is unreasonable.

Now the messy part, and it is genuinely messy.

1. Kickoff walkthrough is 10:00 IST on Monday 12/10/2026, one hour, online.
   Vikram is flying in that morning and lands after lunch, so he cannot make
   it. Vikram, I will record
   it and send you the link, please do not ask me to repeat it live, I know you
   will.

2. The Nashik plant audit sits right on top of week 2 (19-Oct to 23-Oct).
   Vikram is at the plant for four of those five days. That takes UAT-04 and
   UAT-05 out of week 2 completely. Two options, either we prepone them into
   week 1 (tight, the data will still be settling) or we push them to week 3.
   My preference is week 3. Vikram, your call, but please make it this week.

3. Priya has the month end OBIEE agents in the first week so she is part time
   until the 16th. Priya, if that changes tell me and I will redraw.

4. Somebody asked me on Friday whether testers can test at 09:00. You can, but
   the dataset refresh is 06:00 and 14:00 IST, so at 09:00 you are looking at
   the 06:00 picture and not at anything that changed during the day. Please do
   not raise that as a defect, it is by design.

5. Access is by REGION_CODE and there are four roles. If you log in and you can
   only see your own region, that is correct behaviour and again not a defect.
   If you can see everything and you should not, that IS a defect and please
   tell me quietly rather than in the group.

Defects. Please do not mail them to me one by one, I lost two on Friday already.
Everything goes into UAT_defect_log.xlsx which Priya is keeping. One row per
defect, script ID in the first column, and if the script ID is blank I am going
to send it back. Neha has asked that anything raised as a data defect names the
rule it fails, otherwise it goes to the reconciliation pile instead, which is a
different conversation and a slower one.

Capturing that as an action for myself: I will re-issue this grid once Vikram
answers on point 2 and once UAT-11 to UAT-14 have names.

Things I still need, by Wednesday please:
- Vikram: week 1 or week 3 for UAT-04 and UAT-05
- Shalini: confirmation on Meghna for UAT-13 / UAT-14
- Priya: the final tester list with logins, including the north people
- Everyone: diaries.

Thanks all, and sorry again for the delay. It is a four week window and it does
not have much slack in it, so the sooner the grid is frozen

